# Scenario — forward-looking analysis

Part of the [[README|Anchorline vault]].

**Empty by design.** No scenario analysis has been generated yet; this folder is
scaffolded so the boundary exists before there is anything to put in it.

## What belongs here

Analysis of conditions that have **not occurred**. The obvious candidate in this
dataset is the Strait of Hormuz situation, unresolved as of {{ as_of }}: what
each book looks like if it reopens, and if it escalates further.

## What does not belong here

Anything that happened. Those go to `Verified/`.

## Why this is a folder and not a label

A caveat in a sentence can be skimmed past, reformatted away, or lost when
someone copies a paragraph into an email. A directory boundary survives all of
that. `vault_build.py` raises `ScenarioInVerified` rather than writing a
forward-looking fact into the record, so the two cannot merge by accident.

Every note that lands here will carry `confidence: scenario` in its frontmatter
and a warning callout in its body, and will say plainly that it describes
something that has not happened.
